    `horrible_getputpixel()`'s PUT switch fell through unsupported colour types
    (12 of 16 encodings, YCRCB among them) to a default arm that filled `buf`
    with `random()` and stored it: a destination pre-painted 0x11223344 read
    0x56e8857a and 0x38abc4e1 on two runs.  Now the arm clears `ok`, the store
    is guarded by `if (ok)`, the destination keeps what the guest had, and the
    announce is latched once on its own SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR bit.
    
