60: ## 7n-5.  FLOOR OR DEBT -- ARE A DERIVED-COORDINATE ESCAPE AND A VALUE SLICE THE SAME SPECIES?
61: 
62: ### 1. Still live?  PARTLY OVERTAKEN, in both halves, with three wrong records left standing.
63: 
64: * **The doctrinal half was decided on 2026-09-25**, after this question was filed: the flagship D1 ruling on `#549` v6 pinned *"'TESTS' MEANS MASKS OR COMPARES AS A CASE, NOT 'DEPENDS ON'"* -- a relational compare "tests NO bit: its generating set is its three regions, below / at / past the bound", a slice of a compared value crossed with a floor cell is clause (e), and *"grading by consequence would reopen #548"*.  7n-5 asks whether a data-flow test ("flows into the address operand") promotes an untested input to a floor axis; D1 answers no, two weeks after the question.
65: * **The instance half was decided on 2026-09-12 by the committed probe itself.**  `regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py:26-28`: *"CONTRACT -- #519 closure design, 2026-09-12.  This is the controlling coverage contract; older CONTRACT/CLOSED/COMPLETE claims below are historical and are superseded wherever they claim a larger domain or describe missing coverage."*  `:50-51`: *"OUTSIDE: exhaustive coordinates, tile indices, descriptor payloads, raw mode bits, foreground values ..."* -- descriptor payloads ARE the TLB array contents.  The controlling contract already files the gap as clause (e).
66: * **What is left standing against both:** (i) the `sgirandomcolour` note (row text at `scratchpad` line 962): *"the array VALUE is a genuine floor-shaped gap ... Filed as OWED"*; (ii) the probe's historical block `:614-617`: *"the one exception that is genuinely FLOOR-shaped ... filed as owed rather than fixed"* -- formally superseded by the `:26-28` banner (it "describes missing coverage"), but a reader landing there by grep reads it as live; (iii) `regress/pass2_ledger.tsv:159` (the fd15065 receipt): *"Disclosed under (e): bare-predicate mutants with an uninitialised buf; the exact historical M28/M28r edit"* -- the four derived sweeps and the SAMPLED axes the probe discloses at `:593-608` are absent from the receipt's list.  Three L4s.
67: * **Never measured, and that is honest rather than a gap:** table 4 (09-11, M1..M41) and table 5 (09-12, 15 legs) contain no `tileptr & 0xfff00000`, `mode & 1`, `x & 1` or `y & 2` leg; the probe says so (`:607-608` "DERIVED, not measured -- no table has run them").  The round's state is `in work` ("closure records owed"), so the corrections below have their vehicle.
68: 
69: ### 2. The two-minute check that turns "predicted 77/77" into "equivalent by construction".
70: 
71: `src/devices/dev_sgi_re.c` at HEAD: `tileptr = d->re_tlb_[abc][tile_nr] << 16` (`:258-262`), `tileptr = 0x80000000 | (re_linear_a[tile_nr] << 12)` (`:267`), the valid-bit test `if (!(tileptr & 0x80000000))` (`:312`), then **`tileptr &= ~0x80000000;` at `:319`** before the stores at `:374`/`:377`.  Every descriptor the committed probe drives is `0x8001..0x8005` (`:447-449`, `:704`) and the linear tile is `0x10000` (`:95`), so at the guarded store `tileptr` is in `{0x10000, 0x20000, 0x30000, 0x40000, 0x50000}` and `tileptr & 0xfff00000 == 0` on EVERY row.  `if (ok || (tileptr & 0xfff00000))` is therefore textually `if (ok)` on every driven row: 89/89 at HEAD by construction, not by prediction.  The same inspection also classifies it under D1: bit 31 IS a body-tested mask (`:312`), so it belongs to the generating set -- and it is constant-cleared before the store, so the `0xfff00000` slice touches no tested bit at the point of the guard.  Bits 20-30 are untested.  Clause (e), by the letter.
72: 
73: ### 3. Ruling, with its warrant and bound.
74: 
75: **"Closable by a finite row set" is not a discriminator, and the carrier already rejected it.**  On 2026-09-04 the main loop's *"pairs of body-read lvalues over a finite reachable space"* was rejected as SELF-REFUTING: *"the counts' raw value space is 2^32 apiece, so 'finite' does no bounding work ... (a C int is finite)"*.  The measuring seat's floor warrant -- *"pure functions of (x, y, bufdepth, tlb_mode), so the free input set is finite"* -- is that bound back under a new name: `(x, y)` ranges over 2048 x 128 after `y &= 127`, and C1-C4 SAMPLE it (the probe's own vocabulary, `:595`).  And its debt warrant is the same error inverted: *"a slice within an already-driven class is not closable by any finite row set"* (`:610-611`) is true of the FAMILY of slices and false of every member -- `x & 1` dies to one odd-`x` row, `y & 2` to one row with `y` bit 1 set, `mode & 1` to one mode word with bit 0 set, `tileptr & 0xfff00000` to one descriptor `>= 0x8010`.  Finiteness is identical in both buckets: each single predicate is one-row closable; the family of predicates is unbounded.  So it separates nothing, which is why the round graded one species two ways by it.
76: 
77: **The governing discriminator is the one the carrier already carries, read with its bounds.**  (i) Clause (d)'s operand-swap enumeration draws swaps from *fields the guarded BODY READS*, walked up only to the enclosing-function boundary: here `tileptr`, `ofs`, `buf`, `bufdepth`.  Those swaps were all killed at 59 rows (`ok || ofs` 58/59 by `ycrcb x4y1`; `ok || tileptr` by every decline row, since `tileptr` is nonzero everywhere).  (ii) The CELLS owed are the cross-product of the guard's dominating predicates with the body-TESTED partitions of the device-state lvalues the repair path reads (pass 11, 09-04), where "tests" means masks or compares as a case (D1, 09-25).  (iii) A value, bit or slice the body never tests as a case is clause (e), disclosed; consequence orders the debt queue and never promotes to floor (D1: `#549`'s latch x bit was graded (e) although its consequence was the round's own defect).
78: 
79: Applied to `#519`'s survivors, this gives ONE answer for all of them:
80: 
81: | escape | what the body tests on that operand | grade |
82: |---|---|---|
83: | `M30`/`M31` `tile_nr == 0` / `ok \|\| tile_nr` | `tile_nr < 256` only (the `#100` bound) -- relational, three regions; no zero test | (e) |
84: | `M32` `tile_nr_x`, `M33` `y == 0` | `x`,`y` tested `< 0` / `>= 2048`; `y &= 127` runs first; no zero test | (e) |
85: | `ok \|\| (tileptr & 0xfff00000)` -- the TLB array contents | bit 31 tested (`:312`), constant 0 at the store; bits 20-30 untested | (e) |
86: | `x & 1`, `y & 2`, `mode & 1` | bits of compared values / bits read by nothing | (e) |
87: | `M28` nibble carve, `M37` `*color` | `default:` is ONE label for 12 nibbles; `*color` untested | (e) -- already so ruled |
88: 
89: **So the measuring seat's FLOOR grade of the tile-index family was wrong AS A GRADE, and the codex class-closure review of 2026-09-11 was right** (*"BECAUSE THE BODY NEVER TESTS `tile_nr` FOR ZERO, `M30` ... IS NOT A FLOOR AXIS UNDER THE BODY-TESTED-PARTITION RULE -- IT IS CLAUSE-(e) DEBT"*).  The data-flow sentence the seat used (*"flows into the address operand at least as directly as `tlb_mode` does"*) is the 2026-09-09 LABEL clause with its first half dropped: a dispatch LABEL becomes a floor axis when its value flows into a body-read lvalue -- `tlb_mode` is a label the body tests as a case AND flows into `tileptr`; `tile_nr` flows and is not tested as a case.  Flow alone is the transitive-chasing reading the 08-24 bound forbids.
90: 
91: **Harder on the author's leaning, as the brief asks.**  The author leaned YES (floor, L2, a repair owing its own pass).  YES would have reopened a chain the receipt closed ("NO FURTHER PASS IS OWED") on a mutant that no instrument in the tree can see; it would grade by consequence, which D1 refused; and its warrant is the rejected finiteness bound.  And harder on NO, because NO carries a real cost: `ok || (tileptr & 0xfff00000)` keeps the instrument green while re-opening the uninitialised-`buf` store on every real framebuffer tile at a physical address `>= 1 MB` -- the `M30` shape (fix kept on the instrument, open on the world).  The carrier's answer to that is the one it gave at `#549`: severity ORDERS the debt and does not promote it.  So the row is filed at the TOP of this file's coverage debt, below its live defects (`sgirebufuninit`, med), and it costs ONE readback.
92: 
93: **What was legitimately done anyway.**  The 59 -> 77 -> 89 repairs were L1 (pre-ship construction: fd15065 landed 09-12, after all of them), licensed by the round's own choice on a severity finding (98.75% of the screen re-opened by `M30`).  L1 permits strengthening for any reason; only the floor MANDATES.  Nothing the round did was wrong; what it recorded about WHY was.
94: 
95: **EXHAUSTED / SAMPLED: ADOPTED as clause-(e) disclosure vocabulary, with one correction.**  It is exactly what clause (e) asks for -- *"write into the CONTRACT which cells are covered and which are deliberately not"* -- made explicit per axis.  Definitions: EXHAUSTED := every cell of the BODY-TESTED partition of that lvalue is rowed (floor discharged on that axis); SAMPLED := driven at two or more values, with the untested slices and their derived or measured sweeps named.  The probe's `:587` wording "every value in the reachable domain is driven" coincides with the partition definition for `tlb_mode`/`bufdepth`/`color_mode` (tiny domains) and must not be the definition: the next probe with a 2^32 operand could never write EXHAUSTED under it and would write it anyway for a 16-value field the body tests at one bound.  BOUND: a disclosure vocabulary can never DEMAND a row (the carrier's filter rule: *"a filter can reject or repair a row; it can never demand a new one"*), so it cannot grow.  STRUCTURAL LANDING SPOT, per the structure-first rule: the PRETABLE block's GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD check gains one column, "partition the BODY induces on this lvalue" (the codex 09-11 table is the exemplar), and EXHAUSTED/SAMPLED is read off that column rather than asserted.  A template line, not a checker.
96: 
