19356: ### `sgirandomcolour` -- *** `#519` DOES NOT CLOSE.  PASS 2 MEASURED A FLOOR BREACH, 2026-09-11. ***
19357: 
19358: **Six mutants score 59/59 on the shipped instrument and every one writes uninitialised host stack into
19359: guest memory.** `regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260911/` -- 13 builds, 11 instrument runs,
19360: 13 controls.
19361: 
19362:     M30_tilenrdecline   if (tile_nr == 0) ok = 0;       59/59   tile 1, 0x70630000
19363:     M31_tilenrguard     if (ok || tile_nr)              59/59   tile 1, 0x6368696e  <- ASCII "chin"
19364:     M32_tilenrxdecline  if (tile_nr_x == 0) ok = 0;     59/59   tile 1
19365:     M33_tiledorigin     if (linear || y == 0) ok = 0;   59/59   tiled (0,1)
19366:     M28r                the disclosed escape, replicated  59/59
19367:     M37_fgvalue         if (*color == 0xaabbccdd)       59/59
19368: 
19369: **The smallest is eleven characters: `if (ok)` -> `if (ok || tile_nr)`.**
19370: 
19371: *** THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS ARE WHAT MAKE IT A FINDING. *** `|| ofs`, `|| x` and `|| y` each score
19372: **58/59**, killed by exactly one row -- so the probe *does* see geometry. It cannot reach the tile
19373: **index**: its only (4,1) cell is LINEAR, where `x >> 12 == 0`, and a tiled (4,1) would not have
19374: helped either since `x / tilewidth == 0` at every bufdepth.
19375: 
19376: **Severity inverts the usual picture.** At 32bpp a tile is 128x128, so `tile_nr == 0` is
19377: `x < 128 && y < 128`. On the default 1280x1024 framebuffer M30 **keeps the fix over 1.25% of the
19378: screen and re-opens it over the other 98.75%** -- and all 59 rows sit inside the 1.25%.
19379: 
19380: *** THE CAUSE IS A WRONG WARRANT OF MINE THAT HAD ALREADY BEEN REUSED. *** The clause-(d) flow test
19381: was applied **correctly** to `tlb_mode` -- floor axis, via `tileptr` -- and then **stopped at the
19382: ARRAY and never reached the INDEX**. `tileptr = d->re_tlb_a[tile_nr] << 16`, so `tile_nr` reaches the
19383: guarded store's address operand at least as directly as `tlb_mode` does, and `#100` in that same
19384: function already calls `tile_nr` guest-derived and bounds it. My PRETABLE named only `tlb_mode` and
19385: `bufdepth` as `ofs`'s dependencies, while `ofs = 512*y + (x % tilewidth) * bufdepth` contains x and y.
19386: 
19387: **Three reading seats independently found the warrant false before the measurement showed what it
19388: cost**, and one of them made the symmetry argument outright: `M13` (bufdepth), `M14` (linear) and
19389: `M28` (color_mode) are **one guard-weakening shape on three fields**, so *"an instrument-relative
19390: escape is not a contract-relative exemption."*
19391: 
19392: **This is the THIRD consecutive pass finding that shape, so the class-closure rule bites: the next
19393: repair owes the closure in ONE diff, not another cell.** The 16-cell closure was principled and
19394: **incomplete on its own principle**. Reachability is a `sw` to `DE_MODE_DST`, not a driver design
19395: choice.
19396: 
19397: **Also measured, and it trims rather than grows the instrument:** the four `ann cum` rows earn no kill
19398: (delete them and `M5`/`M7` still die via `ann1`/`once`); `tA/tB/tC silent` kill sets are strict
19399: subsets of the matching `ann1` sets; and `ycrcb x4y1` discriminated nothing until the pass-2 mutants
19400: existed. **Rows that carry no kill are score noise.**
19401: 
19402: ### `wdcdiagerr` (MED) -- the premise is INVERTED: `0x01` is the CORRECT code, and the defect is the coupling
19403: 
19404: ATA-2 `:2534` and `:5083`: a device completing diagnostics without error **sets the Error register to
19405: `01h`**. So the value the model writes is right.
19406: 
19407: **The defect is that `d->error` is ONE variable serving TWO registers with opposite meanings** --
19408: `dev_wdc.c:1843` returns it as the **Error register**, and `:594` uses it to raise the **Status**
19409: register's `ERR` flag inside `status_byte()`. The tree's own header shows the collision:
19410: `WDCS_ERR = 0x01` and `WDCE_AMNF = 0x01`, the same number in different registers.
19411: 
19412: **So after EXECUTE DEVICE DIAGNOSTIC the model reports diagnostic SUCCESS in Error and command
19413: FAILURE in Status, simultaneously** -- and `01h` is precisely the value that exposes the conflation. A
19414: one-line change to the diagnostic value would leave `ERR` wrong.
19415: 
19416: ### `wdcpktstatus` -- TWO ROUNDS, not one, and it needs a standard this tree does not have
19417: 
19418: My hypothesis that this and `wdcdiagerr` were one defect is **refuted on a zero: there are NO reads of

